            <ArticleTitle>New technique for superior guiding catheter support during advancement of a balloon in coronary angioplasty: the anchor technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>482-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To get superior guiding catheter support, we tried a new method called the anchor technique. By inflating a balloon in a nontarget vessel and holding its shaft with backward force while advancing another balloon, the anchor effect for the guiding catheter could be obtained and it appeared to be helpful for a balloon or a stent to cross the target lesion.</AbstractText>
